{
  "_readme": [
    "Golden evaluation set. Ground truth is expressed as TEXT MARKERS, not chunk IDs,",
    "so the set stays valid when you change chunk_size, the splitter, or the embedding",
    "model — which are exactly the things you want to measure.",
    "",
    "  relevant_contains  A chunk counts as relevant if it contains ALL of these strings.",
    "                     Matching is case-insensitive, NFKC-normalized (so the PDF's",
    "                     'ﬁ'/'ﬀ' ligatures match plain 'fi'/'ff'), and whitespace-collapsed.",
    "  answer_contains    Markers checked against the generated answer.",
    "  answer_match       'all' (default) or 'any'.",
    "  unanswerable       true when the corpus genuinely cannot answer it. Retrieval is",
    "                     not scored; the model is scored on whether it declines.",
    "",
    "Add cases whenever you hit a real failure — that is what stops it regressing."
  ],
  "cases": [
